==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|en|incumbrance}} {{q|less common since about 1925}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|encombraunce}}, from {{der|en|fro|encombrance}}, from {{m|fro|encombrer}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ɪnˈkʌm.bɹəns/|/ɛn-/|/-bɹən(t)s/}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# Something that [[encumber]]s; a [[burden]] that must be [[carried]].
#* {{RQ:Grey Riders|8|passage=Some consideration was necessary to decide whether or not to leave his rifle there. On the return, carrying the girl and a pack, it would be added '''encumbrance'''{{...|; and after debating the matter he left the rifle leaning against the bench.}}}}
# {{altspell|en|incumbrance||in law: interest attached to a title; dependent}}

